@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor white
actor Student
participant ProfileEditForm as Form
participant ProfilePage as Page
participant profileApi as API
participant handleProfileRequest as HTTP
participant createProfileRepository as Repository
participant "Prisma transaction" as ORM
database PostgreSQL
Student -> Form: Edit permitted fields; Save
Form -> Form: validateProfileDraft; focus invalid control
Form -> Page: handleSave(editable values)
Page -> Page: Disable duplicate saves; retain draft
Page -> API: save(values)
API -> HTTP: PATCH /api/profile (JSON)
HTTP -> Repository: update(body)
Repository -> Repository: validateProfilePatch (shape, keys, values)
alt Invalid request
Repository --> HTTP: ProfileError (400/422)
HTTP --> API: {error: {code, message, fields}}
API --> Page: ProfileApiError
Page -> Form: Field errors; focus first invalid control
else Valid request
Repository -> ORM: $transaction
ORM -> PostgreSQL: SELECT user_id ... FOR UPDATE
ORM -> PostgreSQL: Update supplied scalars; replace supplied interests
ORM -> PostgreSQL: Read complete profile and relations
PostgreSQL --> ORM: Persisted profile
ORM -> PostgreSQL: COMMIT
ORM --> Repository: Complete mapped response
Repository --> HTTP: ProfileResponse
HTTP --> API: 200 ProfileResponse
alt Response received and valid
API --> Page: Confirmed saved profile
Page -> Page: Update view; announce success
else Lost or invalid response
API --> Page: Unconfirmed save error
Page -> Page: Preserve draft; no success announcement
Student -> Page: Check stored values
Page -> API: load()
API -> HTTP: GET /api/profile
HTTP -> Repository: get()
Repository -> ORM: RepeatableRead transaction
ORM -> PostgreSQL: Read profile and relations
PostgreSQL --> Page: Current stored values via response chain
Page -> Page: Show stored values beside retained draft
end
end
note over ORM, PostgreSQL
Any transaction failure rolls back all writes.
Missing profile: 404. Known unavailable DB: 503.
Unexpected failure: sanitized 500.
Concurrent same-field writes use last committed value;
omitted fields remain untouched.
end note
@enduml
